  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the three target docs and the ADR-028 (+Amendment A1) identity model; inventory every Power Pages / B2B-guest statement that is now stale.</step>
    <step>Rewrite `docs/architecture/external-access-spa-architecture.md` to describe SWA hosting (BrowserRouter + navigationFallback + security headers), the CIAM "Ciam" JwtBearer scheme pinned on the `/api/v1/external` group, oid-based Contact resolution, broker-only app-only SPE/Dataverse access + document download, and the retired Power Pages/B2B path.</step>
    <step>Rewrite `docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md` to describe CIAM tenant/app setup, SSPR, `isSignUpAllowed=false`, and the admin-initiated "Invite to Secure Workspace" onboarding flow (no Power Pages / B2B invitation steps).</step>
    <step>Rewrite `docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-SPA-GUIDE.md` to reflect the SWA-hosted SPA, CIAM sign-in + SSPR password set, deep-link behavior, and document download; remove Power Pages hosting/deploy guidance.</step>
    <step>Cross-check all three docs against each other and the code for consistency (authority, scheme name, oid field, endpoint shape); ensure no residual Power Pages-as-current instruction remains.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output>Rewritten `docs/architecture/external-access-spa-architecture.md` (SWA + CIAM + broker-only + retired Power Pages)</output>
    <output>Rewritten `docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md` (CIAM tenant/app + admin-initiated onboarding)</output>
    <output>Rewritten `docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-SPA-GUIDE.md` (SWA-hosted SPA + CIAM sign-in + download)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">All three docs reflect CIAM identity, SWA hosting, and admin-initiated onboarding (invite trigger, SSPR, `isSignUpAllowed=false`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No residual Power Pages-as-current hosting/deploy instructions remain in any of the three docs (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The documented identity model is CIAM (Entra External ID) with Contact resolution by `oid` and the broker-only invariant — not Entra B2B guests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The E-3 direct-Office boundary (per ADR-028 Amendment A1) is noted as out of scope in the architecture doc.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The three docs are internally consistent (authority, "Ciam" scheme, `sprk_externalobjectid`, download endpoint) with no contradictions (negative case — no conflicting statements).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

